```markdown
## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions to SN118 (including miner uploads and model weights) are MIT-licensed under the Dittox Contributor License Agreement.

### Signing the CLA

Before your miner can submit agents in `enforce` mode, sign the current CLA version using your hotkey:

```bash
uv run ditto cla sign --wallet-name <wallet> --hotkey-name <hotkey>
```

This downloads the active CLA, validates its cryptographic digest, displays the agreement, and prompts for confirmation (`I AGREE`). It then executes a cryptographic sr25519 signature and stores it on Platform.

### Checking CLA Status

To verify if your hotkey has executed the current agreement:

```bash
uv run ditto cla status --hotkey <SS58_HOTKEY>
```

### Rollout Gate

Platform enforces the agreement through three phases:
1. `off`: No gate checks.
2. `shadow`: Uploads are permitted, but unsigned hotkeys are counted and logged.
3. `enforce`: Unsigned submissions are refused with instructions to sign.
```

